    "poster_id": 213285,
    "post_rendered": "The two circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d002c517784078b5834f12efe45ad224596f75ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/1169b5ab2cbc837edbec8298a9a56d23dfedca02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" > with the midpoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" > resp. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" > intersect in the two distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> A line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d002c517784078b5834f12efe45ad224596f75ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599041b96dcc5418f1859e57fd8f6f137a93dfac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\neq A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/1169b5ab2cbc837edbec8298a9a56d23dfedca02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" > in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be7f17820d8bb90487591eab8e77c6083317237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D \\neq A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" >.</span> The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda1c9c0c3aced2ecc6440da7894fc44f6c97ffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b76b3cbc94321a383877f826ff906dbbbc9277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DO_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" > intersect in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" >.</span><br>\nProve that the four points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83c710ca83a94d8d4086cce64cc75925d637460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1,O_2,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > are concyclic.",
    "post_canonical": "The two circles $\\Gamma_1$ and $\\Gamma_2$ with the midpoints $O_1$ resp. $O_2$ intersect in the two distinct points $A$ and $B$. A line through $A$ meets $\\Gamma_1$ in $C \\neq A$ and $\\Gamma_2$ in $D \\neq A$. The lines $CO_1$ and $DO_2$ intersect in $X$.\nProve that the four points $O_1,O_2,B$ and $X$ are concyclic. ",
