    "post_rendered": "Determine all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > such that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0e0d3ade918e74de38c9f47bb0fc8373331e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, a_2, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" > defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b2a1f93b11a94b84e7b55f4b4f679aa20e36c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ a_0 = M + \\frac{1}{2}   \\qquad  \\textrm{and} \\qquad    a_{k+1} = a_k\\lfloor a_k \\rfloor   \\quad \\textrm{for} \\, k = 0, 1, 2, \\cdots \\]\"  width=\"444\" height=\"37\" >contains at least one integer term.",
    "post_canonical": "Determine all positive integers $M$ such that the sequence $a_0, a_1, a_2, \\cdots$ defined by \\[ a_0 = M + \\frac{1}{2}   \\qquad  \\textrm{and} \\qquad    a_{k+1} = a_k\\lfloor a_k \\rfloor   \\quad \\textrm{for} \\, k = 0, 1, 2, \\cdots \\] contains at least one integer term. ",
